+| 91 | webgpu: Read the decal atlas through its sRGB view | A view may only use a format the texture declared in viewFormats, and an sRGB view may not carry storage usage. WebGPU lets a view name its own usage to resolve that, but the pinned emdawnwebgpu bindings do not marshal WGPUTextureViewDescriptor::usage (they marshal label/format/dimension/mip/layer/aspect and nothing else), so a view always inherits the texture's - meaning a texture cannot be both storage-capable and readable as sRGB. Storage-capable textures were therefore skipped entirely, which silently cost the decal atlas its sRGB decode: it is storage-capable and is read through an sRGB view, so decals sampled without the sRGB->linear conversion, roughly doubling their mid-tones until they saturated into a hard-edged block (measured as the decal contribution's G/R ratio: 0.691 against 0.318 for a correct decode, 0.600 for none; 0.335 after). The engine names its intent in shareable_formats, so a texture that lists the sibling gets it declared and gives up its storage bit instead - the decal atlas is filled by raster draws and never bound as a storage image. The duplicated sRGB view-usage block in texture_create_shared is folded into one helper and applied to the slice path too | 0 | not yet |
