+| 132 | [shared] renderer: Store SDFGI's packed textures as floats where reinterpretation is unavailable | SDFGI writes radiance as RGBE9995 into R32_UINT and four 4-bit occlusion values into R16_UINT, then samples them through E5B9G9R9_UFLOAT and R4G4B4A4_UNORM shared views - a bit-cast reinterpretation Vulkan, D3D12 and Metal allow and WebGPU's viewFormats (sRGB siblings only) cannot express. New capability SUPPORTS_TEXTURE_FORMAT_REINTERPRETATION (true on the three native drivers, false on WebGPU): without it gi.cpp allocates the light cascades and the probe atlas as RGBA16F and the occlusion as RGBA8, binds them directly, and only the three WRITERS take SDFGI_FLOAT_STORAGE twins that store floats instead of encoding (direct light 2 -> 4 variants, integrate 4 -> 8, preprocess +2: the store twin keeping the k/15 quantization, exact in RGBA8, and the scroll-occlusion twin that reads it back). Every reader - the GI pass, integrate's bounce, direct light's probe feedback, the fog's GI injection, the clustered scene shader's forward GI on transparent surfaces and both debug views - keeps its original float sampling: nothing is degraded and the cone trace stays hardware-filtered. The twins live in disabled groups, so native builds compile nothing extra and run byte-identical GLSL. Cost: RGBA16F doubles the radiance textures on WebGPU (about 45 MB more at four 128^3 cascades) until rg11b10ufloat storage becomes expressible (tint adoption, texture-formats-tier1). Verified natively: packed off = 0.16% and float storage forced on = 0.10% of Cornell pixels differ from the pre-arc editor (run-to-run noise 0.05-0.20%); on WebGPU the SDFGI showcase renders with GI, transparents included, and the SDFGI and probe debug views match the native captures | 9 shared (rendering_device_commons.h, vulkan/d3d12/metal drivers, gi.cpp/h, sdfgi_preprocess/direct_light/integrate.glsl) | not yet |
