+| 199 | webgpu: Keep encoded buffer copies 4-byte aligned | Found by the Dino Pals game session. A 16-bit index buffer with an odd index count has an odd byte size; patch 61 rounded allocations and the XR direct-write path, but the ordered staging copy (boot-created buffers) and readbacks still encoded CopyBufferToBuffer with the exact size, and one invalid copy invalidates the whole frame's command buffer, so every other upload in it was lost (meshes rendered as shards). Copies are now rounded up into the allocation padding when they run to the end of the buffer's requested size; otherwise the aligned part is copied and the loss is reported once. Repro: `xrcost` `oddmesh=1` (get_mesh_arrays() of a 5-segment cone): 'Copy size (330) is not a multiple of 4' and an invalid frame before, 0 errors after. | 0 | - |
