+| 201 | webgpu: Leave staging uploads to the copies that read them | Every buffer_unmap of a CPU (staging) buffer uploaded the whole buffer, although the only GPU readers of a staging buffer are copies and each copy already uploads exactly the bytes it reads. The canvas renderer maps the staging block for each shape it builds (draw_circle, draw_arc, draw_colored_polygon), so an every-frame HUD uploaded the block hundreds of times a frame: the Dino Pals game measured 65 ms of HUD per frame on a phone-class CPU. Unmap of a copy-only buffer (no binding usage, i.e. staging) now uploads nothing; a CPU buffer that can be bound directly is still uploaded (the strict probe binds one as storage). Repro `xrcost` `hud=1` (40 circles + 40 arcs redrawn every frame): flat frame 24.2 to 2.4 ms on desktop; XR eyes pixel-identical. `?nolazyunmap` restores the upload. A free-list buffer pool was tried first and measured no gain, so it is not included. | 0 | - |
