+| 213 | [shared] rendering: Add opt-in asynchronous staging readback dispatch | `RenderingDevice` reads downloads back by mapping the staging buffer when the frame's fence completes, which WebGPU cannot do synchronously. Drivers may now opt in (`buffer_readback_is_async()`, default false) and receive the frame's readback regions through `buffer_readback_async()`, completing each request's callback when the data arrives. Drivers that do not opt in keep the existing path unchanged. Design note: `docs/webgpu-async-readback.md`. | 50 | - |
